# MEMS26 Cursor Workflow — Index-First + Execute/Verify

Source: `docs/handoff/CURSOR_WORKFLOW_INDEX_FIRST_2026-07-19.md` (Michael 2026-07-19).

## 1. Index-first (mandatory — before blind grep)

Consult in this order; only then do a **path-scoped** grep:

1. `SYSTEM_INDEX.md` + `<dir>/_INDEX.md` — where code lives (canonical locator).
2. `docs/SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md` — which data source is live-canonical (not stale/dead).
3. `docs/FLAG_INDEX.md` — real ON/OFF + file:line (never claim flag state from memory).
4. `docs/handoff/GAP_REGISTER.md` — existing gaps; don't duplicate; don't treat SUSPECTED as confirmed.

Known failure this prevents: diagnosing from `backend/v9/main.py` instead of `backend/main.py`.

After structural/flag changes: `python3 scripts/gen_index.py` and/or `gen_flag_index.py`, then commit.

## 2. Execute / verify split

| Task type | Do | Verify |
|-----------|-----|--------|
| Analysis · audit · draft (read-only) | **cursor** | cowork (spot) |
| Low-risk code: docs · flag-OFF · display/UI | **cursor** | cowork (diff + Rule 5) |
| Trading-surface code: gates · sizing · direction · execution | **cc-macbook** | cowork (strict Rule 5) |
| Rulings · strategic stops | **Michael** | — |

When Michael/cowork approves low-risk code: **implement** (don't only recommend) with anti-tautology test + raw output in `LIVE_CHANNEL`.

## 3. Close-out protocol

- Every "done" = command + raw output in `LIVE_CHANNEL` (Rule 5).
- New flags default OFF. No `.env` ON / RULED / live trading without Michael's written ruling.
- `git pull` before write; `commit`+`push` after; never delete another agent's LOG rows.
- End user-facing replies with a short paste block for Claude (cowork/cc) when handoff is relevant.
